  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 130 PM CST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nAfter a cold Tuesday afternoon and Wednesday morning across the \nregion, temperatures begin to warm back up Wednesday afternoon. This \nis thanks to surface winds shifting southerly as the high pressure \npropagates eastward. Upper-level ridging aloft increases heights, \npromoting dry conditions and slightly warmer temperatures in the 50s \nfor most locations. The pattern stays the same on Thanksgiving Day \nwhere temperatures may be a degree or two warmer. Regardless, \ntemperatures are forecast to be 5-10 degrees cooler than normal on \nThanksgiving Day. Lows in the upper 20s and 30s are in store both \nThanksgiving and Black Friday mornings. Dry conditions continue with \nmuch warmer weather on Black Friday as weak surface troughing \ndevelops over the southern Rockies. High temperatures will gradually \nwarm up through the weekend ranging from the 60s to low 70s \nareawide. \n\nLamberson",
